    "result_text": "The build is green: **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** and **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city, exposed on `GET /api/owners/{id}` (and every owner response).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `locality` read-only string field to the `Owner` schema, documenting the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) and the `UNKNOWN` fallback. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `locality` property.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/LocalityDeriver.java`** (new) \u2014 A standalone helper with `static String locality(String city)` implementing the city\u2192region table, returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for a `null` or unlisted city.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(LocalityDeriver.locality(owner.getCity()))\")` and `imports = LocalityDeriver.class` on `@Mapper`.\n\n**Key subtlety I hit and fixed:** My first attempt put `locality(String)` as a `default` method on the `OwnerMapper` interface. MapStruct treated it as a generic `String\u2192String` mapping method and silently applied it to *every* String property (firstName, telephone, email, \u2026), which corrupted the telephone into `\"UNKNOWN\"` and made owner creation fail Bean Validation with a 500. Moving the helper into a separate utility class \u2014 referenced only through an explicit expression \u2014 keeps it out of MapStruct's mapping-method candidate set so it's used solely for `locality`.",
